{title: Come, Ye Faithful, Raise the Strain}
{artist: John of Damascus, tr. John M. Neale / Arthur S. Sullivan}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 113}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 315)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Come, ye faithful, raise the strain
[Em]Of [D]tri[G]umphant glad__[D]__ness;
[A7]God [Em]hath brought forth [D]Isra[Bm]el
[D]In[A7]to joy from [D7]sadness;
[D7]Loosed from Pharaoh’s [G]bit[D]ter [G]yoke
[E]Jacob’s [Am]sons [C]and [G]daugh__[D]__ters,
[G7]Led them with unmoistened foot
[C]Through the [G]Red [Am]Sea [D7]wa[G]ters.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]’Tis the spring of souls today;
[Em]Christ [D]has [G]burst His pri__[D]__son,
[A7]And [Em]from three days’ [D]sleep in [Bm]death
[D]As [A7]a sun hath [D7]risen;
[D7]All the winter [G]of [D]our [G]sins,
[E]Long and [Am]dark, [C]is [G]fly__[D]__ing
[G7]From His light, to whom we give
[C]Laud and [G]praise [Am]un[D7]dy[G]ing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Now the queen of seasons, bright
[Em]With [D]the [G]day of sple__[D]__ndor,
[A7]With [Em]the royal [D]feast of [Bm]feasts,
[D]Comes [A7]its joy to [D7]render;
[D7]Comes to glad Je[G]ru[D]sa[G]lem,
[E]Who with [Am]true [C]af[G]fect__[D]__ion
[G7]Welcomes in unwearied strains
[C]Jesus’ [G]re[Am]sur[D7]rect[G]ion.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Neither might the gates of death,
[Em]Nor [D]the [G]tomb’s dark por__[D]__tal,
[A7]Nor [Em]the watchers, [D]nor the [Bm]seal
[D]Hold [A7]Thee as a [D7]mortal;
[D7]But today a[G]midst [D]the [G]twelve
[E]Thou didst [Am]stand, [C]be[G]stow__[D]__ing
[G7]That Thy peace which evermore
[C]Passeth [G]hu[Am]man [D7]know[G]ing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Alleluia! now we cry
[Em]To [D]our [G]king immor__[D]__tal,
[A7]Who, [Em]triumphant, [D]burst the [Bm]bars
[D]Of [A7]the tomb’s dark [D7]portal;
[D7]Alleluia! [G]with [D]the [G]Son,
[E]God the [Am]Fa[C]ther [G]prais__[D]__ing,
[G7]Alleluia! yet again
[C]To the [G]Spir[Am]it [D7]rais[G]ing.
{end_of_verse}
